## Decisions Made
- Run batch-refine daily at 09:23 UTC with a 45-minute dispatch deadline and retain the 60-minute job timeout.
- Use a workflow-root `knowledge-batch-refine` concurrency group that preserves the active run and coalesces pending triggers to the latest one.
- Treat the 15-minute margin as provisional until wall-clock telemetry validates the final PR/wave tail plus handoff assumption.
- Keep the setup-embedded batch workflow byte-identical to the live workflow via an anchored shell-only parity test.
- Route budget exhaustion through the Post-budget completion gate; only its Pending remains branch enters Graceful Handoff.

## Problems Encountered
- The setup template materially lagged the live workflow and omitted retry input, timeout, permissions, environment, timestamp, token, handoff prompt, and model/effort settings.
- The live/setup action prompt still bypassed the Post-budget completion gate introduced earlier in the plan; a second RED/GREEN cycle corrected both copies.

## Constraints Identified
- Task 4 must remain serial and must not introduce `WAVE_SIZE`; bounded waves belong to Task 5.
- Active PR-atomic work must never be cancelled; labels and commits, not `retry_count`, are durable resume state.
- Workflow and setup template parity includes comments, whitespace, prompts, and permissions, not merely selected values.

## Open Questions
